'''Storm''' is a {{mcat|boss}} along with [[Maxor]], [[Goldor]] and [[Necron]] of [[The Catacombs]] in [[The Catacombs - Floor VII]] and is a disciple of [[The Wither King]].

== Collection ==
Killing Storm and ALL the other Withers increases the Necron collection.
{{:Necron/Collection UI}}
{{CollectionTable|Necron}}

== Boss Fight ==
The boss fight is split into four phases. (Five phases in Master Mode.) There are four Wither Lords: Maxor, Storm, Goldor and Necron. Each Wither will be a boss for a phase that must be killed individually for each phase.

In all parts of the boss fight, lava damages the player for 20% of their max health, as well as launching them upwards in one of 2 ways:

* '''Regular''': You are launched into the air at a standard height ({{InfoNeeded}} blocks).
* '''Super''': Looking upwards at a pitch of -40 or lower triggers a Super lava bounce, boosting you 30% higher than a Regular jump.

=== Phase 1 ===
{{Main|Maxor#Boss Fight}}

=== Phase 2 ===
The factory's second layer is exposed. Storm will now fight after Maxor was defeated in Phase 1. This layer comprises a large hall; a main platform with 4 diorite crushers, an outer ring with control pads for the crushers in the corner, and a ring of lava in between. Wither Miners and Withermancers cover the area, with Wither Guards located on raised platforms. One {{HP|20M}} [[Shadow Assassin]] guards each control pad. Storm will attempt to damage the player with lightning bolts within an area from fireballs thrown onto the ground. Storm will occasionally start a countdown, after which lightning will strike anywhere that is not under an intact crusher and deal 2 bursts of {{Green|75%}} of player's {{Stat|health}} as true damage (Normal Mode), which can one-shot most players. Anything which keeps you alive after taking a fatal hit, such as a {{Item|Wither Cloak Sword}}, can negate the damage (except on Master Mode).

Standing on the control pads raises and lowers the corresponding crusher (except the red crusher, which is broken). When Storm is crushed by a pillar, he will be stunned and become vulnerable for 10 seconds. After this or when his health is drained to {{Green|50%}}, he will enter an enraged state.

The next phase will begin when Storm has been crushed under at least two pillars (purple, green or yellow), and enough damage has been dealt to Storm. Failing to deal enough damage after crushing Storm with all three pillars softlocks the fight (but the amount of damage Storm deals is enough to kill all players.)

